From: steinmarder bounded-MC-wait reset track
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] drm/radeon: evergreen: abort soft reset when MC stays busy

evergreen_gpu_soft_reset calls evergreen_mc_wait_for_idle, logs a
warning on the -1 return, then forges ahead with the GRBM_SOFT_RESET
and SRBM_SOFT_RESET writes.  Writing those reset bits while the
MC bus is mid-transaction is the actual PCI-bus-wedge trigger
observed on CHIP_PALM (Wrestler GPU, Brazos APU, Evergreen /
TeraScale-2 VLIW5).

Bail cleanly via evergreen_mc_resume when the bounded
mc_wait_for_idle times out.  The function is void; the caller
(evergreen_asic_reset) observes that GRBM_STATUS still shows
the hung state and routes to the pci-config reset fallback,
which the bounded-MC-wait safe variant gates further.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 4.7
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/evergreen.c
@@ -3923,9 +3923,16 @@ static void evergreen_gpu_soft_reset(struct radeon_device *rdev, u32 reset_mask)

 	evergreen_mc_stop(rdev, &save);
 	if (evergreen_mc_wait_for_idle(rdev)) {
-		dev_warn(rdev->dev, "Wait for MC idle timedout !\n");
+		/* MC engine is mid-transaction; writing GRBM_SOFT_RESET now
+		 * leaves the MC inconsistent on CHIP_PALM-class silicon
+		 * (Wrestler GPU / Evergreen-TeraScale-2 VLIW5).  Bail cleanly.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(rdev->dev,
+			"aborting soft reset: MC stayed busy after 100ms\n");
+		evergreen_mc_resume(rdev, &save);
+		return;
 	}

 	grbm_reset = SOFT_RESET_CP | SOFT_RESET_CB | SOFT_RESET_DB;
